+# Phase 03.1 Plan 02: Data Ingestion Channels Summary
+
+**PC scan and Gmail read channels with MCP tools for automated profile extraction from local git repos, filesystem, Windows apps, and email metadata**
+
+## Performance
+
+- **Duration:** 9 min
+- **Started:** 2026-03-05T13:48:38Z
+- **Completed:** 2026-03-05T13:57:50Z
+- **Tasks:** 3/3
+- **Files modified:** 4
+
+## Accomplishments
+- PC scan channel analyzes git repos (chronotype, sprint patterns, active projects), file structure (tech stack, devices), and Windows installed apps (categorized by type)
+- Gmail read channel extracts contacts (top 10 by frequency), communication patterns (thread depth, formality), topic clusters, and email activity timing
+- Both channels store results in brain.profile with source='inferred' and differentiated confidence levels
+- MCP server expanded from 10 to 12 tools with pc_scan and gmail_scan registered and dispatching correctly
+
+## Task Commits
+
+Each task was committed atomically:
+
+1. **Task 1: PC scan channel module** - `551c08c` (feat)
+2. **Task 2: Gmail read channel module** - `613bcc7` (feat)
+3. **Task 3: Add pc_scan and gmail_scan MCP tools** - `0e6fa6d` (feat)
+
+## Files Created/Modified
+- `promaia/brain/channels/__init__.py` - Channel package init with module docstring
+- `promaia/brain/channels/pc_scan.py` - PC digital fingerprint scanner (git analysis, file structure, installed apps)
+- `promaia/brain/channels/gmail_read.py` - Gmail inbox reader and profile extractor (contacts, patterns, topics)
+- `promaia/brain/mcp_server.py` - Added pc_scan and gmail_scan tools (10 -> 12 total), handlers, event logging
+
+## Decisions Made
+- Used Windows registry query (`reg query`) instead of deprecated `wmic` for app detection -- more reliable and forward-compatible
+- Gmail connector's `.service` API used directly for thread metadata fetching (format="metadata") instead of full sync_to_local
+- PC scan confidence set to 0.6, Gmail scan to 0.5 -- email patterns are less direct evidence than git commit timestamps
+- App categorization uses simple keyword matching (dev_tools, creative, productivity, communication, browsers) -- keeps it lightweight
+- Gmail thread parsing extracts only: sender, recipients, subject, date, snippet -- never email body text
+- `_run_async` helper handles both sync and async contexts for GmailConnector.connect()
+
+## Deviations from Plan
+
+None - plan executed exactly as written. Plan 01 (onboarding state schema) had already been executed, so tool count was correctly adjusted from 10 to 12.
+
+## Issues Encountered
